### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 02 - API KEY AUTHENTICATION & RATE LIMITING
###
### All /api/v1/* endpoints (except /api/v1/info) require:
###   X-ArcClaw-API-Key: <key>
###
### Default keys from .env.example / DevSecretSeeder (dev mode):
###   internal key : key-internal-changeme    (name: "internal")
###   CI key       : key-ci-changeme          (name: "ci")
###
### In production, override via:
###   ARCCLAW_API_KEYS_INTERNAL=<your-key>
###   ARCCLAW_API_KEYS_CI=<your-key>
###
### Rate limit: sliding window, 20 requests/minute PER KEY.
###   21st request within 60 seconds → HTTP 429
###   Each key has its own independent counter.
###   The CI key and internal key do NOT share a counter.
###
### After Phase 64-B2: DevSecretSeeder is @IfBuildProfile("dev") only.
###   In prod/staging, the dev seeder bean is absent from CDI entirely.
###   The keys listed above only exist in dev/test deployments.
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw running in serve mode
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl    = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey   = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=
# @ciKey      = key-ci-JV/qXAikcUoSCCUsqYxLvNjxW/N3KROQtawg3VRFrJs=
# @invalidKey = totally-wrong-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEGATIVE TESTS - all must return 401
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-1] Missing API key → expect 401
# {"error":"UNAUTHORIZED","message":"Missing or invalid API key","timestamp":"..."}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [AUTH-2] Invalid API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{invalidKey}}

###

### [AUTH-3] Empty API key value → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key:

###

### [AUTH-4] Audit list endpoint without key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###

### [AUTH-5] Audit endpoint with invalid key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{invalidKey}}

###

### [AUTH-6] Skills endpoint without key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills

###

### [AUTH-7] MCP admin endpoint without key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mcp/status

###

### [AUTH-8] DELETE session without key → expect 401
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC BYPASS - these endpoints skip auth entirely
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-9] /q/health bypasses auth → expect 200 (no key needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health

###

### [AUTH-10] /q/metrics bypasses auth → expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/metrics

###

### [AUTH-11] /api/v1/info bypasses auth → expect 200
# ApiKeyAuthFilter explicitly allows paths starting with /info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/info

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POSITIVE TESTS - both keys must be accepted
# AUTH-12 (internal key) appears before AUTH-13 (CI key) - order fixed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-12] Internal key accepted → expect 201
# @name authInternalSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [AUTH-13] CI pipeline key accepted → expect 201
# @name authCiSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}

###

### [AUTH-14] Run a simple agent task with internal key - verifies auth flows through pipeline
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 1 + 1?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [AUTH-15] Access internal session status with CI key → expect 401
# Sessions are associated with the creating key. Another key cannot access them.
# (Only if the API enforces per-key session isolation - verify this behavior.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RATE LIMIT TEST
# ApiKeyRegistry: 20 requests/minute per key (sliding window).
# The 21st request returns HTTP 429 + Retry-After: 60.
# Each key has its own independent counter - CI and internal are separate.
#
# HOW TO TEST:
# 1. Send AUTH-16 request 21 times rapidly (use REST client's "repeat" feature).
# 2. The 21st (or earlier) returns:
#      HTTP 429
#      header: Retry-After: 60
#      body: {"error":"RATE_LIMITED","message":"Too many requests...","retryAfterSeconds":60}
# 3. Wait 60 seconds. Send again → 200 restored.
#
# AUTH-17 tests that the CI key has its own separate rate limit counter.
# Exhaust AUTH-16 (internal), then AUTH-17 (CI) must still return 200.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-16] Rate limit probe for internal key - run this 21 times rapidly
# Expect: HTTP 200 for requests 1–20, HTTP 429 on request 21.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [AUTH-17] CI key has independent counter - must still return 200 after internal is rate-limited
# After AUTH-16 is rate-limited, this CI key request must succeed (200).
# The two keys do NOT share a rate limit counter.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authCiSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLEANUP
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [AUTH-18] Cleanup internal session
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authInternalSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [AUTH-19] Cleanup CI session
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{authCiSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{ciKey}}

###
